│ the physician should have been the correct unit of analysis. INTERVENTION Presence of the error was determined by    │
│ consensus using published criteria. MAIN RESULTS The error was present in 38 articles (70%). The number of study     │
│ physicians was reported in 35 articles (65%). The error was found in 57% of articles that reported the number of     │
│ study physicians and in 95% of those that did not. The error rate was not lower among articles published more        │
│ recently nor among those published in journals with higher rates of article citations in the medical literature.     │
